# ==============================================================================
# .github/large-files.allowlist
#
# Explicit, reviewed exceptions to the 1 MiB per-file limit enforced by
# scripts/checks/check-large-files.sh.
#
# Format: <path> <# justification>
#        Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
#
# Every entry must answer: why must this live in git, and why can it not be
# fetched at build time? Large blobs are downloaded by every contributor on
# every clone, forever — they cannot be removed from history without a rewrite.
#
# RULES FOR MAINTAINERS
#   * Prefer: CDN / object storage / npm dependency / build-time generation.
#   * If an exception is unavoidable, compress first (pngquant, oxipng, svgo).
#   * Review this file at every release; delete stale entries.
# ==============================================================================

# --- Approved exceptions ------------------------------------------------------
# (none yet — the repository is currently under the limit everywhere)
#
# Example entry:
# public/assets/brand/hero@2x.webp   # 380 KiB hero art; cannot be generated at build time
